{20}{I’m glad you asked sir! The Grayhills Public Library was established by the Mayor in 1812. It was created as an attempt to turn Grayhills into a bustling new Technological Economy since the mines had closed.}{I’m glad you asked ma'am! The Grayhills Public Library was established by the Mayor in 1812. It was created as an attempt to turn Grayhills into a bustling new Technological Economy since the mines had closed.}{}{}{}{}
{21}{I don’t understand, how does a Library help?}{}{5}{}{30}{}
{30}{Well, the majority of the miners were uneducated although some did have a small amount of education from schools in Tarant. The only thing most of them were good at was mining. As soon as the mines ran out of silver and iron ore, the very reason for Grayhills existence came into doubt. The Mayor decided that he may as well try and save Grayhills from certain extinction.}{Well, the majority of the miners were uneducated although some did have a small amount of education from schools in Tarant. The only thing most of them were good at was mining. As soon as the mines ran out of silver and iron ore, the very reason for Grayhills existence came into doubt. The Mayor decided that he may as well try and save Grayhills from certain extinction. }{}{}{}{lf0 1}
{31}{So he built the Library to educate the workers?}{}{5}{}{40}{}
{32}{Se he build da Libraree to edukate da miyners?}{}{-4}{}{40}{}
{40}{Precisely sir! It was the belief that if we could turn our simple miners into Technologically savvy individuals by keeping them up to date on all of the latest developments, then Grayhills would attract new business ventures. Unfortunately though, it never occurred to anybody that as the miners were uneducated, it also meant that most of them couldn’t read.}{Precisely madame! It was the belief that if we could turn our simple miners into Technologically savvy individuals by keeping them up to date on all of the latest developments, then Grayhills would attract new business ventures. Unfortunately though, it never occurred to anybody that as the miners were uneducated, it also meant that most of them couldn’t read.}{}{}{}{}
{41}{So what happened?}{}{5}{}{50}{}
{42}{Wat happen'?}{}{-4}{}{50}{}
{50}{Well, there was an attempt to teach them how to read. We did make some good progress for a time... Until new mines opened up in other parts of Arcanum. As such, most of the miners got up and left for the new mining jobs that were available abroad. It seems they enjoyed digging in the dirt. Which makes sense when you think about it, as most of them were Dwarves.}{Well, there was an attempt to teach them how to read. We did make some good progress for a time... Until new mines opened up in other parts of Arcanum. As such, most of the miners got up and left for the new mining jobs that were available abroad. It seems they enjoyed digging in the dirt. Which makes sense when you think about it, as most of them were Dwarves.}{}{}{}{}
{51}{So how did Grayhills survive until this day?}{}{5}{}{60}{}
{52}{How did Grayheels surviyve?}{}{-4}{}{60}{}
{60}{To be honest with you, I’m not really sure. It seems that just enough people stayed around that Grayhills was able to hold on for quite some time. We have become a small tourist destination now but the Mayor still has grand plans for his beloved town. That’s why he’s embarked on an ambitious road paving exercise. It was going quite well too, until the Mummy appeared...}{To be honest with you, I’m not really sure. It seems that just enough people stayed around that Grayhills was able to hold on for quite some time. We have become a small tourist destination now but the Mayor still has grand plans for his beloved town. That’s why he’s embarked on an ambitious road paving exercise. It was going quite well too, until the Mummy appeared...}{}{}{}{}
{61}{Ahhh... Yes, what can you tell me about the Mummy?}{}{5}{}{70}{}
{62}{Okay. So wat you 'no 'bout da Mummy?}{}{-4}{}{70}{}
{70}{The Mummy? I don’t know much about it except that it appeared on the edge of town one day. The whole town is fearful of what it might be doing here. Personally, I think it should be killed. Nasty things these Mummys. In my opinion the undead are better off dead.}{The Mummy? I don’t know much about it except that it appeared on the edge of town one day. The whole town is fearful of what it might be doing here. Personally, I think it should be killed. Nasty things these Mummys. In my opinion the undead are better off dead.}{}{}{}{}
