{120}{Okay, here’s the short version. The Grayhills Public Library was established by the Mayor in 1812 as an attempt to turn Grayhills into a bustling new Technological Economy by educating the miners. Unfortunately however, most of the miners got up and left town for new mining jobs that were available abroad. Grayhills has survived because of a small number of people that decided to stay in town.}{Okay, here’s the short version. The Grayhills Public Library was established by the Mayor in 1812 as an attempt to turn Grayhills into a bustling new Technological Economy by educating the miners. Unfortunately however, most of the miners got up and left town for new mining jobs that were available abroad. Grayhills has survived because of a small number of people that decided to stay in town.}{}{}{}{}
{121}{Okay, can I ask you something else?}{}{5}{}{110}{}
{122}{Okay, me ask you somet'ing else?}{}{-4}{}{110}{}
{130}{Ahhh... Our most recent acquisition! Yes, it was left to us by an adventurer who came through here about a month or so ago. It details the story of a Mummy or something. He seemed to think that that was what was up in the caves. It’s a good read, even if it is a load of hogwash.}{Ahhh... Our most recent acquisition! Yes, it was left to us by an adventurer who came through here about a month or so ago. It details the story of a Mummy or something. He seemed to think that that was what was up in the caves. It’s a good read, even if it is a load of hogwash.}{}{}{}{}
{131}{A load of hogwash?}{}{5}{}{140}{}
{132}{Uhhh... Lode of hogwash?}{}{-4}{}{140}{}
{133}{Great, can I have the book please?}{}{5}{}{160}{}
{134}{Okay, kan me haf' da book pleese?}{}{-4}{}{160}{}
{140}{Well, it says the Mummy may be some old and ancient King who was tricked into being turned into a Mummy by some strange traveller. I mean [she looks at you from underneath her glasses], who ever heard of THAT? As I say, a Mummy is a Mummy because they’re EVIL. Just pure EVIL. And that’s all there is too it.}{Well, it says the Mummy may be some old and ancient King who was tricked into being turned into a Mummy by some strange traveller. I mean [she looks at you from underneath her glasses], who ever heard of THAT? As I say, a Mummy is a Mummy because they’re EVIL. Just pure EVIL. And that’s all there is too it.}{}{}{}{}
{141}{So then how do you think Mummys become Mummys?}{}{5}{}{150}{}
{142}{So how you dink dat Mummys bekome Mummys?}{}{-4}{}{150}{}
{143}{That’s great, now about the book?}{}{5}{}{160}{}
{144}{Uhuh. So 'bout da book?}{}{-4}{}{160}{}
{150}{Hmph! How should -I- know? I’m not a Professor of Mummatology. But this nonsense about ancient Kings, I just reckon that this guy who wrote the book must have been delusional.}{Hmph! How should -I- know? I’m not a Professor of Mummatology. But this nonsense about ancient Kings, I just reckon that this guy who wrote the book must have been delusional.}{}{}{}{}
{151}{Okay, but can I have the book?}{}{5}{}{160}{}
{152}{Uhuh, so kan me haf' da book?}{}{-4}{}{160}{}
{160}{Ahhh... So you wish to read the book? Well, even if it is a load of rubbish it still is a nice story. Very well written I must say. Uses all the appropriate vowels and consonants and all in the right place too!}{Ahhh... So you wish to read the book? Well, even if it is a load of rubbish it still is a nice story. Very well written I must say. Uses all the appropriate vowels and consonants and all in the right place too!}{}{}{}{}
{161}{Uhhh... Vowells and konsonants?}{}{-4}{}{170}{}
{162}{Yeah, that’s great, so can I have it?}{}{5}{}{180}{}
{163}{Okay, so kan me haf' it pleese?}{}{-4}{}{180}{}
{170}{Er... Never mind. It’s just nicely written.}{Er... Never mind. It’s just nicely written.}{}{}{}{}
{171}{Okay. So Kan me haf’ da book?}{}{-4}{}{180}{}
{180}{Well.... [She looks at you for a moment, as if to size you up] I have a small problem that I need taken care of first. It’s a minor thing, something that I’m sure you would be able to handle. If you do it for me, I’ll give you the book you want.}{Well.... [She looks at you for a moment, as if to size you up] I have a small problem that I need taken care of first. It’s a minor thing, something that I’m sure you would be able to handle. If you do it for me, I’ll give you the book you want.}{}{}{}{}
